# Top 10 Behavioral Questions — ERI Interview Prep

Each question has two versions:
- **SHORT** — 1-2 sentence elevator version for quick recall
- **STAR** — full structured answer for deep follow-up

---

## 1. The Conflict — "Tell me about a time you disagreed with a technical decision made by a lead or manager. How did you handle it?"

**SHORT:**
I found a JavaScript bug in Google Analytics that was causing IE users to drop off — my lead dismissed it as only 2% of traffic, so I pulled the revenue numbers and showed it was costing over $10,000 a month. The fix got prioritized.

**STAR:**
- **Situation:** While proactively reviewing our Google Analytics conversion funnels at Ultra Mobile, I noticed IE browsers had a significantly higher drop-off rate than other browsers. I traced it to a JavaScript compatibility bug that was breaking the experience for IE users — a browser that accounted for about 2% of our traffic.
- **Task:** Make the case to prioritize the fix when my lead's initial read was that 2% of traffic wasn't worth the sprint capacity.
- **Action:** Rather than argue the technical merits, I went to the revenue numbers. I took our average monthly revenue, isolated the IE traffic segment, and calculated what that drop-off rate was costing in lost conversions — it came out to over $10,000 a month. I brought that number to my lead instead of a traffic percentage. A percentage is easy to dismiss, a dollar figure is not.
- **Result:** The fix got prioritized and shipped. The lesson I carried from that conversation was that technical decisions land differently when you translate them into business impact first. Data doesn't just help you build things — it helps you get the right things built.

